hi my name is victor baldus and today  i'm going to teach you how to create  proper margins for your design when you  write a letter you don't start on the  outer edge of the paper the same applies  for placing columns on an artboard to  make your text legible and pleasing for  the eye you need to add white space  around your columns we call these  margins but how much margin do you add  to a book  to a business card a flyer there is no  standard way to do this but there are  some methods we can use like the thumb  margin system where the margin should be  at least a thumb wide to not obscure any  text or images this works great for  books mobile phones and other devices  another way to create margins that are  pleasing to the eye is to create a set  of diagonal lines like this  and then there's a type system where you  create a system of margins based on the  size of the type you are using the goal  of creating margins is to create a  layout where text and images has room to  breathe and ultimately create a solid  hierarchy in your design if you want to  learn more about margins design systems  and grids i've created the grids and  layouts kit where i outline the process  to create beautiful layouts i've also  included templates with the most common  grids so you can create them with ease
 

